# Dependencies & build output — reinstalled / rebuilt inside the image
#
# `**/` is load-bearing, not tidiness: a .dockerignore pattern with no `**` is
# anchored at the context root, so a bare `node_modules/` left every
# `packages/*/node_modules` in the build context. pnpm fills those with symlinks
# — on Windows, junctions — and the remote builder's tar cannot classify one:
# `archive/tar: unknown file mode ?rwxr-xr-x`, and the deploy dies at ~36 MB of
# context transfer with nothing pointing at the cause (2026-08-13). Nested
# installs only appeared once the repo grew workspace packages.
**/node_modules/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets & runtime data — never bake into the image
.env
.env.*
data/

# Caches, VCS, local tooling
.git
.github
# Agent-session state; worktrees under here carry full checkouts + pnpm
# junctions that break the remote builder's tar (deploy failure 2026-07-27)
.claude/
**/.turbo/
**/.vitest-cache/
**/coverage/
.vscode
.idea
scratchpad/

# Local-only UI/QA artifacts — Playwright scratch.
.playwright-mcp/

# Working docs (plans, specs, notes, GPT/owner reviews) — dev-only, never referenced
# by the app; keep them out of the deployed image. Subsumes the old
# ux-audit-assets exclusion (the whole developer-notes folder is now excluded).
docs/developer-notes/

# Generated/eval imagery under docs — regenerable; text docs (.md) stay.
docs/**/*.png
docs/**/*.jpg
docs/**/*.jpeg
docs/**/*.gif
docs/**/*.webp
docs/**/*.avif
docs/**/*.bmp
docs/**/*.tif
docs/**/*.tiff
